{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e","id":929989,"title":"Lodge of Wires (2e)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-11T15:09:24-07:00","id":929989,"title":"Lodge of Wires (2e)","content":"Techwolf/hackwolf is one of my favourite character concepts. Probably why I love Iron Masters so much. With all the Ghost in the Shell stuff going on with the Technology gift I thought to create a character who was a member of the Lodge of Wires (Tribes of the Moon pg 138). This character is for a supernatural Taskforce crossover type game (Vampire, Mage, Werewolf and Beast), so I sort of wanted to create a Ghost in the Shell/Serial Experiments Lain type feel with it (though it already had most of that going on to begin with so the lore is mostly unchanged). I have a tech spirit retainer (specifically communication networks), and totemic empowerment. Drones to Iron Slave, etc.<br /> <br /> This is what I got so far, let me know what y'all think. I am not quite sure on the Lodge Sorcery influences being what they are, and I'm debating whether the lodge should even have Lodge Stronghold. Lorehouse might suffice, though I like the idea of a hackerwolf who got in over her head being able to lay low at some tech fortress for protection until the heat dies down and she can construct a new cover. Obviously the lodge lorehouse is a website of some kind.<br /> <br /> Also, a friend has implied that he thinks the Sacred Hunt effect is incredibly strong, so I wanted feedback on that. Initially its effect was tracking people by the frequencies of their devices (as with Taste of Blood), but that seemed silly since most devices have GPS' as well. Next it had an effect of being impossible to pick up on surveillance, but again that seemed unnecessary for a lodge that probably doesn't spend too much of it's time outdoors. So I ended up with this, which I like, but am looking for feedback on.<br /> <br /> While I don't necessarily feel it has to change, the ban seems pretty easy to maintain, especially with the lodge fetish (which is a direct port from 1e) so I might look to bump that ban up a bit and am very open to suggestions.<br /> <br /> Also, still working on Amplified Frequency and refining the idea.<br /> <br /> And lastly I'm looking to revamp the gift of Information, which was pretty useless in 1e but is still a strong concept to me. If anyone has ideas on that or has already homebrewed a version I'd love to hear/look/borrow them. <div align=\"center\"><u><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Lodge of Wires</b></span></u></div> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Bonds</b></div> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing: </b>The Lodge of Wires erases all traces of the lodge member from the world's computers. Lodge members also achieve exceptional success on Computer and Science rolls on 3 successes instead of 5.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>Develop new ways to fuse technology and spirit magic<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must always have access to the internet or other communication network.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>Sacred Hunt</b></div> <br /> <br /> While on Sacred Hunt, The Lodge of Wires grants your character the ability to use Gifts that require visual sight, even when viewing a location, object or person through lenses or other video technology. When viewing through surveillance equipment, the lodge member may project their wolf or spirit senses as though present at the location, this ability even extends to recorded video. <div align=\"center\"><b>Tools</b></div> <br /> <br /> The Lodge of Wires has access to the Lodge Connections, Lodge Lorehouse, Lodge Sorcery and Lodge Stronghold merits, and may choose Sorcery Influences from Internet, Surveillance and Knowledge. Lodge Strongholds exist in many of tech hubs and burgeoning tech hubs in the United States, such as San Jose (California), Dallas (Texas), Seattle (Washington), New York (New York) as well as globally in Bangalore (India), Geneva (Switzerland), Beijing (China) and Guangdong (China).<br /> <br /> <b>Lodge Fetish: Digital Eye</b> (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Most Wireheads create or inherit an Eyepiece shortly after becoming full members of the lodge. The werewolf must bind a spirit servant of the Digital Eye into a cutting-edge smartphone with runes of the future etched into the case. All versions of the Eyepiece can call any phone or access the Internet from anywhere. A lack of phone signal is no problem, neither is the Gauntlet. Each Eyepiece also monitors news sources, flagging news stories that might be of interest to its owner. More importantly, the Eyepiece is the only way that a Wirehead can access the secure computer networks of the Lodge of Wires. The three-dot version of this fetish gives a werewolf a measure of the Digital Eye\u2019s true power. He can use his Eyepiece to see through any surveillance camera within a mile. If he selects a specific target, he can seamlessly track that target using any camera in range<br /> <br /> <b>Lodge Rite: Amplified Frequency</b> (\u2022)<br /> <br /> Amplified Frequency amplifies the range of a wirehead's spiritual frequency to emanate not just from her, but from her packmates as well - greatly extending the range and effectiveness of her gifts.<br /> Symbols: Amplification, networks, power, technology<br /> Sample Rite:<br /> Cost: 1 (network resonant) Essence per packmate involved.<br /> Action: Extended (10 successes; each roll represents 15 minutes)<br /> Duration: 3 Months<br /> Success: Allows the lodgemember to use packmates as well as themselves for calculation of the range of any gift or fetish.<br /> <br /> (Example, Pack Awareness = sense packmates within 1 mile, amplifies to sense packmates within 1 mile of Franky or any packmate with Franky\u2019s amplified essence.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I reused most of the 1e stuff, but some of it had to change with the new direction of the lodge.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxK0La5plUm8NHRURzF0OUN2bms/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the version I currently have up.</a><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 07-16-2016, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T16:01:08-07:00","id":930010,"title":"","content":"The ban doesn't depends on the werewolf, what's more, someone using the Purity Facet of Technology can endlessly fuck with them.<br /> <br /> Sure, give them all the lodge merits. No, not really. Pick two like the other ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T16:13:31-07:00","id":930017,"title":"","content":"Well bans are meant to be exploitable. Someone should be able to fuck with you if they know your ban and have the capability to exploit it. Besides, the Fetish kind of circumvents that, which was actually my concern. It becomes much less exploitable with the Fetish.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm pretty sure there is no guideline to how many lodge merits a lodge should be able to provide beyond 'what makes sense'. From what I remember all the lodges in The Pack have access to a different number of merits. Garm has 1, Apollo has 3. So I'm not really concerned with the number.<br /> <br /> But if what you're really saying is that you think one or more of those merits are inappropriate, then that is much more sensible and actually helpful. Especially if you could provide some reasoning. Lodge Armory, for example, definitely would not make sense.<br /> <br /> I think I might agree that Lodge Stronghold is probably not necessary or even particularly thematic, so even though I gave my reasoning for including it, it might not make the final cut. I do think the stipulation of providing specific locations (predicated on the idea of 'tech hubs') does kind of make it more reasonable, however.<br /> <br /> Also, full disclosure, I'm not sure I understand the first clause of your first sentence.<br /> <br /> Edit: Thanks for responding, though. Hope I'm not hurting your feelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 07-11-2016, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T16:38:15-07:00","id":930034,"title":"","content":"Wow.<br /> <br /> I've been a big fan of the Lodge of Wires for a while and I really like this. I don't think the Sacred Hunt benefit is too strong, considering the amplification of their normal senses. The ban seems fine as well.<br /> <br /> Really well done.<br /> <br /> You're just missing one thing, the totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T17:28:45-07:00","id":930049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e?p=930010#post930010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ban doesn't depends on the werewolf, what's more, someone using the Purity Facet of Technology can endlessly fuck with them.<br /> <br /> Sure, give them all the lodge merits. No, not really. Pick two like the other ones.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Forget about supernatural means. Your Comcast conexion goes down for a minute and you have already broke your bane. Not to mention all the areas on a city where the signal is poor/noexistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T17:32:51-07:00","id":930052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e?p=930034#post930034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow.<br /> Really well done.<br /> <br /> You're just missing one thing, the totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, man. I'm a huge fan of the lodge also. And the Siskur Dah is so great thematically, so I'm glad you agree.<br /> <br /> The original write-up has the lodge Totem as The Digital Eye, but it doesn't really give a lot of info. I don't want to post much directly from the book, but this is pretty much all it says:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The Lodge of Wires pays lip service to Red Wolf, but members save their reverence for the Digital Eye, a vastly powerful spirit of the future. Only a few Wireheads know that their patron is also the Lord of Surveillance, and the lodge his chosen warriors.&quot; and &quot;Once her training is complete, the recruit petitions the Digital Eye. If she\u2019s deemed incompatible, she never hears from the lodge again \u2014 and if she goes looking, powerful spirit magics obstruct her path. If the Lord of Surveillance believes that she will advance his agenda, he erases all traces of her from the world\u2019s computers, welcoming her to the lodge.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> It's able to erase info from the world's computers, as well as prevent access to whatever web presence the lodge has. This to me suggests a powerful spirit, Rank 4-5. More likely 5. Powerful enough to represent the Big Brother type surveillance and have it's sphere of influence spread wide.<br /> <br /> It also sounds to me like a spirit of Surveillance masquerading as a spirit of the Future, or a spirit of Surveillance that manifests with a Futuristic bent. I'm imagining a controlling, obsessive, potentially paranoid/conspiratorial/secretive spirit that is using the Uratha it binds to the lodge to ensure that it will be the strongest tech spirit when our dystopian future finally arrives. There will be tech spirits aplenty, and a huge power boom, so if it is to survive it needs to be prepared.<br /> <br /> Looked at generously, it might want to create a future where it can manage the growth of tech spirits, because of their immense influence on the direction of humanity. It might be nurturing or just monitoring their growth, so that it can react appropriately. It might even go so far as to use its influence and Uratha to prevent particularly dangerous or malevolent tech spirits from taking hold of humanity's imagination. To guide it in the right direction.<br /> <br /> The flipside of this, of course is that it might be creating a future where it can reap the rewards of the resonant essence that Humanity creates. It might be gently urging it in that direction, and taking down all comers to the throne. Afterall, it was sitting on the throne long before the palace was built around it. There's a lot of really juicy stuff there as far as plot hooks.<br /> <br /> To quote the book <i>&quot;Tomorrow\u2019s Son (leader of the lodge) believes in the Panopticon, a particular future where everyone is tracked and watched at all times. Despite all he\u2019s tried, most lodge members don\u2019t think his particular future is the best option. There\u2019s plenty of room for conflicting opinions, especially from characters who have a different view of the future. Other groups and lodges study the future in the short and medium terms, but the Lodge of Wires is the scary bastard thinking two steps beyond the cutting edge. Nobody likes the Wireheads, but for now they\u2019re a necessary evil.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> So I was thinking Influences in Knowledge, Internet, and Surveillance. Maybe Computers instead of Knowledge or Internet. Mostly because I don't really know how Influence: Future would work, or if that's even possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 07-11-2016, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T17:53:27-07:00","id":930061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e?p=930049#post930049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Forget about supernatural means. Your Comcast conexion goes down for a minute and you have already broke your bane. Not to mention all the areas on a city where the signal is poor/noexistent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would a member of the Lodge of Wires be in a city where the signal is poor/nonexistent?<br /> <br /> And why would your home internet be your only connection when you have a ban about keeping connected to the internet?<br /> <br /> And guys, I will direct you to the Lodge fetish: &quot;All versions of the Eyepiece can call any phone or access the Internet from anywhere. A lack of phone signal is no problem, neither is the Gauntlet. &quot;<br /> <br /> Which boils the ban down to 'don't lose your Eyepiece' once you've made one. So I was more concerned with that end of it. And I definitely didn't consider it particularly strict or unmanageable before the fetish, but you all seem to think it is. I guess because it's sort of not entirely under your control? It's something that you could fail at through no fault of your own. So I see why it might feel particularly strict, I guess. Though I feel like there are enough measures that could be taken or safeguards that could be put in place for a cautious Wirehead. My worry was more that it swings too much in the other direction once the fetish comes to play. Any ideas, then? Maybe you are prevented from hunting, or must behave in some particular way whenever you are not connected to the internet? I don't have any immediate ideas for that one.<br /> <br /> The idea behind the ban was essentially the ban requires for you to always have access to Lodge's secure website (which I will try to develop more specifics about), and for other lodge members to always be able to contact you. And that you never be off the grid - as that wouldn't sit well with a spirit of surveillance. So thematically I feel like it's fine. I'm not sure how much of a problem it is as it stands right now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T18:13:02-07:00","id":930069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e?p=930061#post930061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I definitely didn't consider it particularly strict or unmanageable before the fetish, but you all seem to think it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not everyone. I, for one, think it is a perfectly thematic ban. I don't think people are objecting because it is unmanageable, and if I am wrong in that then the people objecting for that reason are incorrect. I think people might be objecting due to ease of exploiting, which is different than managing it without interference. I think having a ban which is exploitable in a very apparent way is good given how amazing their fetishes and lodge gift is. Having two devices on seperate networks and a home that includes dial up (hardwire phone lines are the most reliable internet connection, and nothing in the ban says it has to be fast internet) and maybe convincing your pack to have a technology spirit that has the influences needed to protect you internet connection and you've done some major mitigation to potential risks. Protecting your ban from being exploited <u>should</u> take work. Also shameless link to amazing allies for members of this lodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-11-2016, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T18:23:26-07:00","id":930075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e?p=930061#post930061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would a member of the Lodge of Wires be in a city where the signal is poor/nonexistent?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because shit happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e?p=930061#post930061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And why would your home internet be your only connection when you have a ban about keeping connected to the internet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because shit happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e?p=930061#post930061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And guys, I will direct you to the Lodge fetish: &quot;All versions of the Eyepiece can call any phone or access the Internet from anywhere. A lack of phone signal is no problem, neither is the Gauntlet. &quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you give them an irrelevant ban.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T19:32:40-07:00","id":930121,"title":"","content":"That's rather dismissive, Ephsy. 'Shit happens' is a good reason for all bans to be tested. But the Lodge doesn't seem to be just random people with internet access, they're clearly invested more into it. And even with the Eyepiece, one is relying on an object that can be destroyed by an enemy who wants to make you break your ban, which is basically the main reason bans exist.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5279\" data-vbnamecard=\"5279\">Amravanti</a> That's great, and very fitting with the nature of lodges, and the spirit. In this, do you think it is more like the Temple of Apollo, where they work on granting the spirit better access to the world? Basically, what do they do when a member of the Lodge? Are they focusing their sacred hunts on enemies of technology and those who would try to regulate or limit it? Are they hunting down those who would find ways to avoid surveillance, or going into lands that would otherwise not have the ability and start building the infrastructure for Digital Eye to be at home there? Maybe Digital Eye speaks to them directly, acting sort of how the God Machine does to Angels, having them take out certain threats and protect others as part of some grander plan for the future?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-11-2016, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T23:10:30-07:00","id":930190,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a><br /> All good points! I do also like how much the ban mirrors the 21st century anxiety of being disconnected from the internet. Whenever I leave my phone at home or it dies on me I feel that weird, anxious sense of disconnection. So yeah, I think I do like the ban. Like you said, an appropriately paranoid and cautious Wirehead would take the necessary steps to reduce the risk of violating the ban due to sabotage or happenstance. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a><br /> Any suggestions? Those all seems like good reasons to keep it. Challenging, promotes a sort of obsessive planning to ensure that the ban isn't violated, which is very in-theme, I envision a sort of home base of sorts - back up generator, multiple computers on multiple networks, dial up, tangles of wires running across the walls and floor, screens everywhere, a rack filled with seven different phones from seven different providers. Can never be too careful.<br /> <br /> All in theme. As far as the fetish though, I had the same concern, though I think it's not so safe as to make the ban irrelevant. If you rely on one item you're being pretty reckless. But like I said, open to suggestions.<br /> <br /> Hope I haven't hurt your feelings or anything.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a><br /> Also a very good question, I haven't completely defined a purpose or sacred prey for the lodge. I would think they would take as their Sacred Prey... hm. Those are all good suggestions, actually. Enemies of progress or technology is a good candidate, I think that's the most straightforward and sensible. Both human and supernatural, of course. Which has the side effect of expanding the Digital Eye's influence in those areas.<br /> <br /> But I do like the idea of moving into places and building infrastructure for the totem, and direct mandates from the totem. Maybe I'll start a fluff/lore write-up and see which direction feels most sensible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T15:25:21-07:00","id":930548,"title":"","content":"Current changes in my head involve dropping Lodge Stronghold as I've been debating, and creating an associated mystery cult.<br /> <br /> Something like:<br /> <br /> <b>The Panopticon</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Panopticon is a hacker group whose mandate involves promoting the advance of technological advancement. The Lodge of Wires has had it's claws in the group since it's inception, and members of the Lodge of Wires may purchase the Mystery Cult Initiation or Mystery Cult Influence merit in regard to The Panopticon, and in fact many Wireheads were members of The Panopticon before being brought into the fold.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022) </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">New recruits are tasked primarily with DDoS attacks and doxxing politicians or influential personalities who oppose technological progress. There is no hand holding in the Panopticon, as members are immediately thrown into the deep end and are expected to drown or learn to swim, and quick. They gain the <b><u>Hacking</u></b> specialty in Computers, if the initiate already has the specialty (and most do before joining) they gain the <u><b>Area of Expertise</b></u> merit instead.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022)</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Members who stick around this long have learned the value of patience. One mistake, one sloppy hack or miscalculation could bring the whole house of cards down. They gain the </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Patient</u></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">merit. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022) </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While still not trusted with the Panopticon\u2019s vast stores of information, members at this level now have access to the group\u2019s secure channels, and at this stage are likely to have contact info or other ways of reaching a few members of the group for advice or collaboration. They gain the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u><b>Hobbyist Clique</b></u> (Computers) </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">merit.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this stage members gain access to large stores of collected data </span></span><b><u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Library</span></span></u></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022\u2022\u2022) merit with a focus on Computers. The Lodge of Wires keeps close watch of The Panopticon\u2019s ranks, at this stage if the member is Uratha or Wolfblooded, he is most likely approached for initiation into the Lodge.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Only the most trusted and influential members of The Panopticon, or members of the Lodge of Wires, have access to this level. The Lodge of Wires is willing to let a portion of their true knowledge and data slip to humans. Members now gain access to the </span></span><u><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lodge Lorehouse</span></span></b></u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022\u2022\u2022) merit, even if they are not members of the Lodge. Though stores of knowledge that involve the Uratha, Spirits or other supernatural phenomena are still off limits to humans.<br /> <br /> Or, Humans with this level of dedication to the cause must be supported where necessary, Members gain access to the <u><b>Lodge Connections</b></u> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022) merit, even if they are not members of the Lodge. Though resources that involve Uratha, Spirits, or other supernatural phenomena are still off limits to humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> Very rough draft at this point. Literally just wrote it right now, but critique is welcome.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 07-12-2016, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T17:07:35-07:00","id":930601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e?p=930190#post930190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as the fetish though, I had the same concern, though I think it's not so safe as to make the ban irrelevant. If you rely on one item you're being pretty reckless. But like I said, open to suggestions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe losing contact with your Eyepiece already counts are lacking internet connection, right? All someone has to do is remove it from your grasp, done. Hell, a tied character might be considered &quot;lacking internet access&quot; since it can't access internet without manipulating the devices near it. It is a very interesting Ban, since it seems hard to maintain overall, but easy if you are an obsessive lunatic that plans every step before leaving home (like accounting for free hotspots, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T17:12:48-07:00","id":930603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e?p=930601#post930601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe losing contact with your Eyepiece already counts are lacking internet connection, right? All someone has to do is remove it from your grasp, done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd expect the Eyepiece wouldn't be used widely in public, <a href=\"http://eyetap.blogspot.com/2012/07/physical-assault-by-mcdonalds-for.html\" target=\"_blank\">considering people's reactions to things like that</a>, though to be fair as a werewolf someone is literally risking their hand trying to take something off of your face. Even if they did, you're saved by having a cell or smartphone in your possession.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Plus it looks like 'Eyepiece' might just be a term, referencing the Digital Eye. It looks like it can just be made from a smartphone or other device. It doesn't have to be something over your eye.<br /> <br /> Anyways, unless you're bound somewhere or traveling in a technologically backward area, you'll still have access to the internet or a communications network through phones, internet cafes, the devices of passerbys you can take from and so forth. But when a hunt calls for you to go into some sort of mine or back woods or other area where you will be cut off you will have to find another way. It's like the Thousand Steel Teeth, who have to sleep a mile from where they slept the night before. It's easy to do in most cases, even without a car a werewolf can likely walk a mile in a day, but if they're locked up someplace they're going to have an issue. You could never spend a week on a small tropical island.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-12-2016, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T01:03:05-07:00","id":931237,"title":"","content":"Yeah, as you said the Eyepiece is just a reference to the Digital Eye, I think. It is a bit misleading because one imagines some kind of eyewear. I was tempted to change it for that reason, but I figured I should stay as true to the original as possible.<br /> <br /> And yeah, thanks for the feedback everyone. Definitely feeling a lot more comfortable with the ban.<br /> <br /> Here's where I'm at right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxK0La5plUm8NHRURzF0OUN2bms/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxK0La5plUm8NHRURzF0OUN2bms/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxK0La5plUm8NHRURzF0OUN2bms/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxK0La5plUm8NHRURzF0OUN2bms/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T03:07:14-07:00","id":931901,"title":"","content":"I'm interesting if there should not be at least part of overlap with Seer's of Throne Ministry of Panopticon with the Mystery Cult...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T03:27:49-07:00","id":931905,"title":"","content":"Ruh roh. I was not aware there was a Mage Panopticon Mystery Cult. I'll have to looking into that and maybe changing the name.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T03:43:02-07:00","id":931908,"title":"","content":"There is WHOLE MINISTRY named Panopticon. To be correct, Pantechnicon is also one, only smaller...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T05:16:15-07:00","id":931936,"title":"","content":"They're both named that for a reason. While you could change the name because of it, similar to something like demon it's unnecessary, as it's possible for two things created by two groups of people and inspired by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panopticon\" target=\"_blank\">real life</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panopticism\" target=\"_blank\">concepts </a>to use the same name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T11:25:54-07:00","id":932114,"title":"","content":"The ban is too harsh for a Lodge. Also, the does the blessing work constantly, or only the once? If it works constantly it's probably too powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T13:57:19-07:00","id":932188,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6783\" data-vbnamecard=\"6783\">notanautomaton</a> The blessing of erasing all records I was thinking would happen just upon entering the lodge. After that you're on your own. The exceptional success rolls of course would be a constant.<br /> <br /> As far as the ban being too harsh for a Lodge I'd love to hear more about why. I think I'm pretty settled on it at this point. My GM has already approved it, and no other ideas immediately jump out at me anyway. I feel bans should be commensurate with blessings and other benefits a lodge provides and so it seems appropriate to me. Also, if you have any suggestions, please.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> Yeah, I think nofather might be right on this one. The names were probably chosen for the same reason so I don't think it's too strange for the two organizations to exist without any overlap or interaction. The only issue is continuity OCD, which is a very real thing in my heart. So I'll see if anything better pops out at me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T16:09:58-07:00","id":932242,"title":"","content":"If you want, I can have a look over this at some point and give some feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T17:03:25-07:00","id":932256,"title":"","content":"Very much yes, please and thanks.<br /> <br /> And I am comfortable with your being as blunt as necessary.<br /> <br /> And a weigh in especially on the ban issue would be greatly appreciated.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also know that I am currently trying to refine the sacred prey thing as it's a bit scattered and I don't think I've fully represented the motivation of 'The Herd Shall Not Know' thing yet. But any help there is also super welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 07-16-2016, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T17:59:27-07:00","id":932283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e?p=932256#post932256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also know that I am currently trying to refine the sacred prey thing as it's a bit scattered and I don't think I've fully represented the motivation of 'The Herd Shall Not Know' thing yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could make them anti-government surveillance hacktivist. Vigilance (Person of Interest) style.<br /> <br /> The more pervasive such surveillance becomes, the harder it is to Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 07-15-2016, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T18:09:11-07:00","id":932288,"title":"","content":"That's the exact opposite of the direction I've taken it so far, though. That'd be a complete about face.<br /> <br /> And using technology to fight the creep of technology seems to muddy the waters a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T10:40:24-07:00","id":932559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e?p=932188#post932188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as the ban being too harsh for a Lodge I'd love to hear more about why. I think I'm pretty settled on it at this point. My GM has already approved it, and no other ideas immediately jump out at me anyway. I feel bans should be commensurate with blessings and other benefits a lodge provides and so it seems appropriate to me. Also, if you have any suggestions, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at the other Lodge bans. They're typically relatively easy to get around, like having to have two places to sleep at least a mile away from each other, or having to use the body of everything you kill. This requires you to be constantly connected, and is easy for any enemy to exploit, be it through destroying their cell phone or just going somewhere where there's no reception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T11:08:53-07:00","id":932568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e?p=932559#post932559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at the other Lodge bans. They're typically relatively easy to get around, like having to have two places to sleep at least a mile away from each other, or having to use the body of everything you kill. This requires you to be constantly connected, and is easy for any enemy to exploit, be it through destroying their cell phone or just going somewhere where there's no reception.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about downgrading the Ban so that it doesn't have to be maintained 24/7?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T11:12:29-07:00","id":932569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e?p=932568#post932568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about downgrading the Ban so that it doesn't have to be maintained 24/7?</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work. Maybe something like 'must spend at least one hour per day online?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T11:14:44-07:00","id":932572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e?p=932569#post932569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could work. Maybe something like 'must spend at least one hour per day online?'</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that's both manageable and thematically appropriate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I second this.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, perhaps you should remove Lodge Lorehouse as an option in the Tools section. It doesn't seem to fit the Lodge, in my opinion. Not to mention the Temple of Apollo never even went beyond three such Merits in your write-up. Alternatively, you could scratch out Lodge Sorcery instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 07-16-2016, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T04:21:12-07:00","id":932863,"title":"","content":"I thin the Ban needs to change, and the Sacred Hunt is too overpowered.<br /> <br /> For Ban, I'd suggest: Lodge members must always try to connect to an available wireless network broadcasting in their local range. If multiple networks are available, the Uratha can choose which to connect with.<br /> <br /> This gives a Ban that is easy enough to follow, but can cause some difficulty to the Uratha if they're in an area with prey-controlled wifi, and risk giving away their presence by connecting to their network. (In other words, fun drama.)<br /> <br /> For Sacred Hunt, I'd go with something you suggested in your third paragraph. Members of the Lodge can unerringly track the signal of any wifi-capable device carried by the prey. They achieve Exceptional Success on three successes (instead of five) when hunting such prey, and always gain at least one success per roll to track the prey, even if no dice roll successes. Lodge members can still choose Dramatic Failure on a failed tracking roll, though such an action is considered a grievous insult to the totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T13:42:32-07:00","id":933026,"title":"","content":"Ok, so, some feedback!<br /> <br /> \u200bFirst things first, from the fundamentals:<br /> - Remember that 2e Lodges are quite different beasts to 1e ones. They are more focused.<br /> - Don't worry too much about balance etc initially - get the core ideas nailed down then refine and iterate the mechanics from there.<br /> <br /> It's important to know:<br /> - WHAT/WHY/HOW the Lodge refines the Sacred Hunt. Not just in mechanical terms, but in symbolic and contextual ones. How is this Lodge about the Hunt? This is absolutely core to what a Lodge is. Remember - a Lodge is a <i>cult </i>of the <i>hunt</i>. Thus far, I can see the Lodge of Wires are clearly about networked stuff - so why are they using data networks etc to hunt? Is there a specific type of prey they're after? Why do adherents care enough to swear themselves to the service of an alien being over the matter?<br /> - WHO the totem is and WHAT they want. Unlike in 1e, where Lodge totems could often be rather sidelined or just bits of descriptive fluff, 2e Lodge totems are involved meddlers. From what I recall, the Lodge of Wires was a bit better about this already in that it hada totem with an agenda - but it needs reiterating in a 2e form. What does the Digital Eye get its minions to do? In what way does it share their focus on the Lodge's particular refinement of the sacred hunt? If the Lodge adherents are the Digital Eye's 'chosen warriors' - what are they chosen <i>for</i>?<br /> <br /> Once these sorts of questions are clearly answered, it's much easier to build the rest of the Lodge on top of that foundation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e#post929989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blessing: </b>The Lodge of Wires erases all traces of the lodge member from the world's computers. Lodge members also achieve exceptional success on Computer and Science rolls on 3 successes instead of 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first one should be a very high-dot Rite (note that a <i>less extensive </i>version of this is already a 5-dot Tribe-specific rite) or a specific boon that the Digital Eye can deliver for its most favoured Lodge members under dire circumstances - the sort of thing that involves burning colossal political capital and exerting spiritual power across the <i>entire world</i>. Why would the totem offer this blessing in the first place? Isn't it the place of the Lodge adherents to be cleaning up their traces with their own capabilities, skills and powers? At best, this should really be a localised power. I can see why an exceptional on 3 for Computers given the Lodge's subject matter, but Science seems out of place. I would suggest scrapping the entire Blessing and starting again from scratch with something more interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Aspiration: </b>Develop new ways to fuse technology and spirit magic </div> </div> </div> Is this something the Digital Eye cares about? Isn't it more about the developments of how tech and spirit interact, rather than specifically trying to fuse tech and spirit magic? How do you see this aspiration affecting Lodge members in play?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Ban:</b> Must always have access to the internet or other communication network. </div> </div> </div> It's not very interesting, to be honest. I'm not concerned about how hard it is to meet or how vulnerable it makes Lodge members - those are both <i>good </i>things as they add character and interesting situations in-play - but this is almost always going to come down to 'I carry a bunch of network-enabled devices on me' and have no further impact on the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Sacred Hunt</b></div><br /> <br /> While on Sacred Hunt, The Lodge of Wires grants your character the ability to use Gifts that require visual sight, even when viewing a location, object or person through lenses or other video technology. When viewing through surveillance equipment, the lodge member may project their wolf or spirit senses as though present at the location, this ability even extends to recorded video. <div align=\"center\"><b>Tools</b></div> </div> </div> </div> While interesting, it's a) missing the actual sacred hunt parameters (in general, with some exceptions, this sort of stuff should only work vs the hunt's prey) and b) I'm not sure what the refinement of the sacred hunt they're going for here is in-character. I need to know more about the What/Why/How of their sacred hunt approach and beliefs to say if this really fits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lodge of Wires has access to the Lodge Connections, Lodge Lorehouse, Lodge Sorcery and Lodge Stronghold merits, and may choose Sorcery Influences from Internet, Surveillance and Knowledge. Lodge Strongholds exist in many of tech hubs and burgeoning tech hubs in the United States, such as San Jose (California), Dallas (Texas), Seattle (Washington), New York (New York) as well as globally in Bangalore (India), Geneva (Switzerland), Beijing (China) and Guangdong (China). </div> </div> </div> Sorcery and Stronghold don't seem to really fit. I'd suggest look at Connections and Lorehouse, decide which one you absolutely couldn't do without for the Lodge concept, and keep that one; see if the Lodge can work without the second one. You want to refine and focus the Lodge concept at this stage; piling on as many Lodge Merits as you can just muddies it and leaves me unclear as to what this Lodge is about and what it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Lodge Fetish: Digital Eye</b> (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Most Wireheads create or inherit an Eyepiece shortly after becoming full members of the lodge. The werewolf must bind a spirit servant of the Digital Eye into a cutting-edge smartphone with runes of the future etched into the case. All versions of the Eyepiece can call any phone or access the Internet from anywhere. A lack of phone signal is no problem, neither is the Gauntlet. Each Eyepiece also monitors news sources, flagging news stories that might be of interest to its owner. More importantly, the Eyepiece is the only way that a Wirehead can access the secure computer networks of the Lodge of Wires. The three-dot version of this fetish gives a werewolf a measure of the Digital Eye\u2019s true power. He can use his Eyepiece to see through any surveillance camera within a mile. If he selects a specific target, he can seamlessly track that target using any camera in range </div> </div> </div> So it's a magical iphone - seems fine for 2 dots. I'd suggest making the 3-dot one work its power via modifying a Facet in a Gift that you think is appropriate for the Lodge, encouraging adherents to get that Gift so they can benefit from the 3-dot one. Note that currently the power actually gives you no way to know how many or where any surveillance cameras within a mile are.<br /> <br /> Actually, I'll be blunt - I'd just cut this fetish entirely. I think we can assume 'magical iphone' will be common enough amongst the Wireheads, but why go so far as to write it up as a fetish? It's only the 3-dot version that's actually interesting. I am always looking for ways to cut wordcount, reduce down, focus; so cut the 2-dot version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Lodge Rite: Amplified Frequency</b> (\u2022)<br /> <br /> Amplified Frequency amplifies the range of a wirehead's spiritual frequency to emanate not just from her, but from her packmates as well - greatly extending the range and effectiveness of her gifts.<br /> Symbols: Amplification, networks, power, technology<br /> Sample Rite:<br /> Cost: 1 (network resonant) Essence per packmate involved.<br /> Action: Extended (10 successes; each roll represents 15 minutes)<br /> Duration: 3 Months<br /> Success: Allows the lodgemember to use packmates as well as themselves for calculation of the range of any gift or fetish.<br /> <br /> (Example, Pack Awareness = sense packmates within 1 mile, amplifies to sense packmates within 1 mile of Franky or any packmate with Franky\u2019s amplified essence.) </div> </div> </div> I dislike it. I don't see how it matches the Lodge, tbh - the use of 'amplified frequency' comparisons with networks just comes across as a clumsy comparison that doesn't make a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I reused most of the 1e stuff, but some of it had to change with the new direction of the lodge.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxK0La5plUm8NHRURzF0OUN2bms/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the version I currently have up.</a><br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div> And of course only now I see this link with the whole write-up, because I am a lemon :P<br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, awesome, there's a nice clear statement about their sacred prey:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lodge takes as its sacred prey anyone, human or otherwise, that works to impede or halt the progress of technology. The Lodge of Wires also concerns itself greatly with a particular tenet of the Oath of the Moon, \u201cThe Herd Must Not Know,\u201d and goes to great lengths to hide and erase instances of its breach. </div> </div> </div> Ok, with that clarity, it strikes me that the sacred hunt benefits make no sense. They do nothing to help hunt peope impeding or halting the progress of technology, and nothing to help hide or erase breaches of the Oath.<br /> <br /> Next, the actual totem. Again, the write-up here makes me think that the current Aspiration doesn't really make much sense. It doesn't actually reflect what the Digital Eye is interested in or wants, even when filtered through the Uratha lens. The Digital Eye doesn't seem to give a shit about fusing tech and spiritual magic - it seems to care about <i>control</i>.<br /> <br /> Also, just wanted to point out one bit in the Membership section:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bAt least two members of the lodge use brainwashing techniques to bring new recruits around to their way of thinking. </div> </div> </div> This is a bit of a nonsense line, in part because I have no context whatsoever for how significant 'two' is here. Just say 'Some members of the Lodge', and ideally offer some sort of hint as to what sort of brainwashing techniques you mean.<br /> <br /> I'm not keen on the name of the Panopticon mystery cult - not because of cross-over with Mage or whatever, but because it doesn't really fit the group. They're about opposing those who would stop progress - but the name 'panopticon' is about total vision, seeing all, and specifically it comes from a context to do with <i>prisons</i>. I guess they could run with the metaphorical notion that they have broader vision than those they fight or whatnot, or that info can't be hidden from it, buuuut it feels like they should have a name that is about progress or something else more suited to their goals. They don't seem to be about 'you can't hide from our sight', they're about 'ushering in our idea of the glorious technological future by dealing with those who would oppose it'.<br /> <br /> I'm also incredibly leery of the 5-dot benefit, and indeed anything that would offer Uratha-only benefits from Lodge merits to non-Uratha.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T14:54:58-07:00","id":933076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e?p=933026#post933026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course only now I see this link with the whole write-up, because I am a lemon :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I must admit, I missed the link as well when giving my thoughts, above.<br /> <br /> Right, then:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lodge takes as its sacred prey anyone, human or otherwise, that works to impede or halt the progress of technology. </div> </div> </div>That's cool. Though the <i>Siskur-Dah</i> benefit is irrelevant to this, as Chris said. My idea above, is also irrelevant to this concept, so please disregard.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lodge of Wires also concerns itself greatly with a particular tenet of the Oath of the Moon, \u201cThe Herd Must Not Know,\u201d and goes to great lengths to hide and erase instances of its breach. Lodge members monitor thousands of conspiracy blogs, paranormal blogs and more traditional news sources in search of violations. Those reckless few (Uratha or otherwise) who pose repeated risks to the Oath, as well as the unlucky humans who learn too much, often find themselves the targets of the Lodge\u2019s\u2019 Sacred Hunt \u00ad after which any mention of them soon disappears without a trace. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, this also makes no sense. Either the Lodge celebrates human development of technology, or it punishes those who develop technology that risk the Oath of the Moon. You can't have it both ways. From what you've written, the Lodge should have great interest in this tenet of the Oath, as they struggle between encouraging humans to invent, culling those who impeded, while knowing doing so risks their race's exposure.<br /> <br /> Welcome to Lodge life. It's meant to be difficult. If you don't want the responsibility, don't join a Lodge. :/<br /> <br /> With this in mind, the Lodge's hunt needs to focus on those who impede tech. Consider a bonus against those who impede technology's progress. Research companies that lock promising tech behind patents because the older tech generates more profit. CEOs who initiate hostile takeovers of start-ups because their innovations are more efficient, or render the old tech obsolete. A bonus to tracking or killing these people would be appropriate. As a twist, perhaps the Sacred Hunt allows the Uratha to track any tech that it being hidden from the world, and once that's found, identify the specific individuals that need to be dealt with.<br /> <br /> Also be aware that spirits aren't human. The Digital Eye is going to expect its adherents to expose new tech regardless of whether it helps or hurts humanity. Once the tech is available to all, the humans will determine this through use. Many may die, but that's not the spirits's concern. The humans may quickly decide that the tech shouldn't be used, and that's fine. Either way, humanity will progress through the innovation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ban:\u200bMust always have access to the internet or other communication network. </div> </div> </div>Okay, so the ban is also thematically inappropriate for the Digital Eye. It presumes the spirit only cares about internet, and while it does have a massive current interest in the internet, it's not its only focus.<br /> <br /> A more appropriate Ban would be: <i>Members of the Lodge must try to use any new technology they encounter</i>.<br /> <br /> With their hunt leading them straight to new technology, this will of course be risky, but see above about how easy Lodge life is meant to be.<br /> <br /> Plus everything Chris said. Those are my thoughts for now. (Having read the linked write-up.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T22:33:34-07:00","id":933736,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Daaaamn. Thanks for all the feedback, both of you. Clearly you both are very correct about muddied concept/identity. I sort of knew as much myself, I suppose. I just went back through the Lodge creation rules and examples in The Pack and I realize now that even though I trimmed down a lot from the original 1e version, I hadn't fully grasped just how focused 2e Lodges are meant to be and I just ended up with a generic Technology/Futurist lodge (phones, internet, surveillance, cyberpunk, etc.). I'll be working on refining the concept and figuring out which parts are really central to the lodge identity and translating that to the Blessings, etc.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So in my head I\u2019ve refined the lodge to being about surveillance, and the </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>control</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> of surveillance - with an eye toward the future. Like Acro said, the totem seems to be very about control. The element of watching and encouraging development of technology I think is pretty central and complements the idea of \u2018watchers.\u2019 (though if I can\u2019t get those components to feel married and cohesive I may cut even further) but I\u2019m removing the bit about </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>stewarding</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> mankind toward its future (or encouraging \u2019benevolent\u2019 tech spirits\u2019) as clearly that is not really anything a spirit would be concerned about. Though this still may be the face the lodge presents to the outside world. </span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/#\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Acrozatarim</u></span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Fetish and text was a straight copy from the 1e version so I didn't really consider altering it at all, but I agree that there isn't really much use for the 2 dot version, and it's a major oversight to not have a way to locate the cameras it is supposed to affect.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Similarly, the effect of wiping records of the Uratha upon joining the lodge was one of the 1e version's benefits that I thought was thematically cool and left in. I\u2019ll figure out if it even has a place anymore. Might be too much even for the Mystery Cult final benefit, not sure. (Speaking of: Name change imminent)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As far as including Science in the blessing, I guess that was a vestige of the general tech/transhumanist angle that is largely unnecessary, all things considered. It was there for a reason, but i was thinking too broadly at the time.</span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/#\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Bunyip</u></span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> I was worried the 'impedes progress' aspect of the lodge was </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>too</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> narrow. This is likely why I added the bit about The Herd Must Not Know, though it made sense to me at the time. I agree there is some conflict, especially in the idea of killing humans who have done </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>too</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> well.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I think I\u2019ll use your sacred hunt idea as a jump off point and try to figure out the rest from there, you put into words a lot of stuff I was having trouble identifying as solid goals. Thanks for that.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I had also been trying to wrap my head around a Fetish idea I\u2019ve had, that bestows a full working knowledge of any item the Uratha has deconstructed using Unmake (Technology/Glory Facet). Perhaps with the ability to reconstruct it after. Though that might not have a place in this lodge and might be a personal character Fetish. Though I can't even think of an actual item to tie it to.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anyway, thanks a lot guys. Very useful stuff. I'll continue to work on it.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 07-19-2016, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T01:06:04-07:00","id":933772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929989-lodge-of-wires-2e?p=933736#post933736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So in my head I\u2019ve refined the lodge to being about surveillance, and the </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>control</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> of surveillance - with an eye toward the future. Like Acro said, the totem seems to be very about control. The element of watching and encouraging development of technology I think is pretty central and complements the idea of \u2018watchers.\u2019 (though if I can\u2019t get those components to feel married and cohesive I may cut even further) but I\u2019m removing the bit about </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>stewarding</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> mankind toward its future (or encouraging \u2019benevolent\u2019 tech spirits\u2019) as clearly that is not really anything a spirit would be concerned about. Though this still may be the face the lodge presents to the outside world. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds A LOT like Panopticon Seers of <b>Mage</b> line. Maybe some crossover would be good in here. If you go this route, I may even used Lodge in my London Mage as Panopticon is large antagonist in there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}